= The Left Stands Out

On 16 June the First All-Russia Congress of Soviets opened in Petrograd. Over 1,000 delegates were present, 777 with a vote. The SRs and the Mensheviks hold a majority. When Tsereteli declared that "there is at present no political party in Russia that would say: give the power into our hands", Lenin shouted from the floor: "There is such a party!" The Left SRs were silent, and applauded.

Within the SR delegation, which is the largest in the hall (about [+ seat_sr +] delegates), the Left SRs number perhaps [+ lsr_delegates +]. They are enough to be heard, and not enough to decide.

- @power: Vote with the Bolsheviks: all power to the Soviets.
- @bridge: Propose a government of all the socialist parties.
- @discipline: Vote with the SR delegation.

@power
on-arrival: {!
Q.lsr_backs_bol = 1;
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: 6, rel_ally: -4, soviet_democracy: 1});
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: 3, workers: 3});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 3, -3);
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 0, 8);
!}

A motion for Soviet power was introduced by the Bolsheviks and lost. The Left SRs voted for it. The SR leaders called it a betrayal of the party, and the Bolsheviks have begun to speak of the Left SRs as their natural allies.

@bridge
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_bol: 3, rel_lsr: 5, rel_ally: 2, soviet_democracy: 2});
RO.boost(Q, {workers: 1, soldiers: 1});
RO.fac(Q, 'rightdef', 2, -2);
RO.fac(Q, 'defencist', 1, 0);
!}

The Left SRs proposed that the Congress take power in a coalition of all the socialist parties. The Congress did not take it up, but the Menshevik Internationalists, who proposed the same, noted that there was somebody else on their side of the hall.

@discipline
on-arrival: {!
RO.add(Q, {rel_ally: 4});
RO.fac(Q, 'intl', 0, 8);
RO.boost(Q, {soldiers: -2});
!}

The Left SR delegates voted with the SR delegation, as the party's rules require. It was a matter of discipline. The pro-Bolshevik wing noticed, and so did the Baltic Fleet.
